{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789174262,"nonce":"9ghw7u1l+Dz1k4RKZ9k37vkbasw=","message":"Root cause, from the diagnostics on PR #4 (run 34661726601): the JIT half of the smoke test is the tiered runtime in compiled-only mode, so its traps are the CRANELIFT tier's, and cranelift/codegen.rs armed them with _setjmp(buf) alone. ASH_TRACE_THROW showed the frame word as 0x7ff6223920a1 on every throw -- a code address in ash.exe left in rdx by hlp_setup_trap_jit -- so longjmp unwound with SEH through Cranelift frames that carry no .pdata, and the process died with nothing on stderr.\n\nThe binding and the LLVM address, where this issue said to look, were fine: on the runner, hl::_setjmp reaches VCRUNTIME140.dll code starting with mov [rcx],rdx, _setjmp(buf, NULL) then longjmp(buf, 7) round-trips with frame=0x0, and jmp_buf is 256 bytes at 16 alignment. crates/ash/tests/win_setjmp.rs pins that and runs in the Windows job.\n\nFixed in 04cc113: Cranelift passes the null frame when its call conv is WindowsFastcall; throw_impl clears the frame word before longjmp on Win64 for traps an HDLL armed with the C macro (which passes a real frame); aot_smoke prints exit codes in hex. With the Cranelift change alone the Windows job passed on the branch (run 34662624765, all nine jobs green). The bench manifest's claim that --mode jit is a whole-module LLVM compile was what sent the search to the wrong tier; corrected in the same commit.","files":null}]}